<article class="env-lemma" id="0BM6">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BM6">Lemma <span data-tag="0BM6">58.19.6</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0BLF" data-tag="0BLF">58.19.1</a>. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$H^1_\mathfrak m(A)$ and $H^2_\mathfrak m(A)$ are annihilated by a power of $f$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$A$ is henselian or more generally $(A, (f))$ is a henselian pair. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the restriction functor $\textit{FÉt}_ U \longrightarrow \textit{FÉt}_{U_0}$ is fully faithful. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0BLI" data-tag="0BLI">58.19.4</a> we may assume that $A$ is a Noetherian complete local ring. (The assumptions carry over; use Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ALZ" data-tag="0ALZ">47.9.3</a>.) By Lemma <a href="/tag/0EL8" data-tag="0EL8">58.17.1</a> the result follows from Algebraic and Formal Geometry, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EKS" data-tag="0EKS">52.15.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>